ASoC: codecs: wcd937x: count the RX clock users with a DAPM supply

wcd937x_rx_clk_enable() returned early when the count was already set,
so the count never went above 1, while every RX1/RX2/RX3 power down
called wcd937x_rx_clk_disable(). With the headphones (RX1 + RX2) the
first power down switched the RX analog clocks and bias off under the
second path, and the second one logged "clk already disabled". On SM4375
(Xiaomi Redmi Note 12 5G) every PipeWire start, which opens and closes
each UCM device once, logged about ten of them.

Make the RX clocks an "RXCLK" supply widget that RX1, RX2 and RX3 depend
on, as wcd938x does, and let DAPM do the counting. The per path digital
clocks are still switched off in the RX power down, now before the shared
analog clocks instead of after them for the last path, which is what
wcd938x does too.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

